1
00:00:31,099 --> 00:00:32,734
You know this guy.

2
00:00:32,984 --> 00:00:34,550
Everyone does.

3
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:39,836
The Discord mod: tiny crown, huge power, zero chill.

4
00:00:40,086 --> 00:00:44,996
Today we find out where he came from, and whether he's
even real.

5
00:00:49,283 --> 00:00:53,449
First, a fact that gets lost in the jokes.

6
00:00:53,699 --> 00:00:57,471
Most Discord moderators are volunteers.

7
00:00:57,721 --> 00:01:02,663
No salary, no benefits, and usually no training.

8
00:01:02,913 --> 00:01:09,753
A server owner picks someone active, hands them a
role, and says "keep it clean."

9
00:01:20,053 --> 00:01:27,095
Spam, scams, fights, trolls, and the occasional person
who is just having a rough day.

10
00:01:27,345 --> 00:01:31,430
All of it handled between school, work and sleep.

11
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:43,156
So why does the internet picture a power-hungry tyrant
instead?

12
00:01:43,406 --> 00:01:46,330
It comes down to four reasons.

13
00:01:54,017 --> 00:01:58,879
A mod role comes with real buttons: mute, kick, ban.

14
00:01:59,129 --> 00:02:03,787
Online, there is almost no check on how they get used.

15
00:02:04,037 --> 00:02:08,227
No manager, no handbook, no appeals form.

16
00:02:08,477 --> 00:02:12,991
Give anyone that button and some will press it too
fast.

17
00:02:19,791 --> 00:02:24,712
When a mod quietly stops a scam, nobody notices.

18
00:02:24,962 --> 00:02:29,407
When a mod bans someone, a whole channel watches.

19
00:02:29,657 --> 00:02:33,263
Good moderation looks like nothing happening.

20
00:02:33,513 --> 00:02:36,576
Bad moderation makes a screenshot.

21
00:02:42,876 --> 00:02:51,245
In many servers the new mod is whoever is online the
most, or whoever the owner already knows.

22
00:02:51,495 --> 00:02:53,630
Plenty of them are great.

23
00:02:53,880 --> 00:03:00,913
Others are learning how to handle authority in real
time, in public, with an audience.

24
00:03:07,113 --> 00:03:13,045
The internet's favorite hobby is turning a few bad
stories into a character.

25
00:03:13,295 --> 00:03:20,700
A handful of screenshots become a joke, the joke
becomes a meme, and the meme becomes a type.

26
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:27,823
After that, every strict mod is proof, and every kind
one is an exception.

27
00:03:31,717 --> 00:03:34,722
Here is the uncomfortable part.

28
00:03:34,972 --> 00:03:38,270
The stereotype is not just a joke.

29
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,260
It feeds itself.

30
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:55,589
When the only reward is respect, the role becomes part
of a person's identity.

31
00:03:55,839 --> 00:04:00,795
A challenge to the rules starts to feel like a
challenge to them.

32
00:04:08,595 --> 00:04:14,143
After the hundredth troll, everyone starts to look
like the next one.

33
00:04:14,393 --> 00:04:16,272
Jess was not a troll.

34
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:19,841
Tyler just stopped being able to tell.

35
00:04:24,941 --> 00:04:33,239
If a ban feels unfair and there is no way to challenge
it, the banned person has one outlet left: complain

36
00:04:33,209 --> 00:04:35,225
loudly somewhere else.

37
00:04:35,475 --> 00:04:39,744
That is where most of the stories you have seen came
from.

38
00:04:44,844 --> 00:04:48,511
Burnout drives out the patient mods first.

39
00:04:48,761 --> 00:04:52,230
The ones who enjoy control stay the longest.

40
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:59,119
So the stereotype slowly becomes truer, even though it
started as unfair.

41
00:05:27,517 --> 00:05:28,838
Meet Priya.

42
00:05:29,088 --> 00:05:32,314
She is the reason your server had a calm morning.

43
00:05:32,564 --> 00:05:36,765
No thank-you, no screenshot, no applause.

44
00:05:37,015 --> 00:05:39,674
Just a clean channel when you woke up.

45
00:05:40,174 --> 00:05:48,218
The best moderation is invisible, which is exactly why
the bad moderation is what everyone remembers.

46
00:06:28,039 --> 00:06:33,115
The mod stereotype is real, and so are the people
behind it.

47
00:06:33,365 --> 00:06:39,842
Next time you are about to roast one, remember the 3
a.m. raid you never saw.
